$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2-Amino-4-bromo-N-(((2S*,5R*)-5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-methyl)benzamide
(rac-8b). DIPEA (1.15 mL, 6.94 mmol) and HATU (1.32 g, 3.47 mmol) was
added to the suspension of 2-amino-4-bromobenzoic acid (5) (0.5 g, 2.31
mmol) in dry DCM (20 mL), and the mixture was stirred at rt for 15 min.
Then 5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methanamine (rac -7b) (0.36 mL, 3.47
mmol) was added, and the mixture was stirred at rt for 2 h. The solvent
was then removed in vacuum, and the remaining residue was purified by
column chromatography (1/1 = EtOAc/PE),
2-Amino-4-bromo-N-(((2S*,5S*)-5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-methyl)benzamide
(rac-8c). Prepared in analogy to compound rac-8b. Yield 0.35 g (97%),
colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.74-1.83 (m, 1H), 1.87-1.96
(m, 1H), 2.16-2.24 (m, 1H), 2.35-2.42 (m, 1H), 3.35-3.42 (m, 1H),
3.75-3.81 (m, 1H), 4.42 (qd, J = 3.5 Hz, 6.7 Hz, 1H), 5.01 (dd, J = 6.3
Hz, 8.2 Hz, 1H), 5.63 (brs, 2H), 6.45 (brs, 1H), 6.75 (dd, J = 2.0 Hz,
8.2 Hz, 1H), 6.84 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.19 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H),
7.25-7.29 (m, 1H), 7.31-7.37 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 29.6,
35.3, 43.5, 78.5, 80.9, 114.7, 119.5, 119.5, 125.6, 126.5, 127.5, 128.4,
128.6, 142.7, 149.9, 168.7. MS (ESI) m/z (relative intensity): 375.3
(100%), 376.3 (16.8%), 377.2 (72.9%), 378.2 (29.9%).
